From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:38:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "Stop the liquid flow scan and the sense cache from
 allocating"

Measured -0.18% TPS, 2/6 pairwise wins, at 30,000 golems with four bots. A flat null.

The change did what it claimed: it removed roughly a quarter of everything the server
thread allocates, plus a frame carrying 2.3% of its samples. The tick rate did not move.
Bump allocation into a TLAB is close to free and G1 absorbed the garbage at this rate, so
allocation volume is not what this server is short of - and EntitySenses.clearSensingCache
was another self-time frame that was not the work underneath it.

Kept in history rather than deleted: the next person to read an allocation profile of this
server should see that the largest sites on it were already tried.

